            <ArticleTitle>[Retrograde mammary-coronary anastomosis and its place among other methods of myocardial revascularization].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>7-13</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Under consideration is a special kind of mammary-coronary anastomosis--a retrograde mammary-coronary anastomosis, first suggested by the authors. An anteretrograde mammary-coronary anastomosis was performed in 104 patients, a retrograde one--in 6. The use of a retrograde mammary-coronary anastomosis yielded favourable results, which in some cases are remained for 4-5 years.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
